        <h1 class="post-detail__title">19th Annual Tin Cup Challenge Launches June 12 — Teton Valley Invited to Give Local!</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/19th-annual-tin-cup-challenge.webp" alt="19th Annual Tin Cup Challenge Launches June 12 — Teton Valley Invited to Give Local!" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>Driggs, ID, June 12, 2026 — The&nbsp;<strong>Community Foundation of Teton Valley</strong>&nbsp;is proud to launch the&nbsp;<em>19th Annual Tin Cup Challenge</em>, a collaborative fundraiser that unites neighbors across the valley to support the good causes that make life in the Tetons vibrant, resilient, and connected.</p>

<p>From&nbsp;<strong>Friday, June 12, through Friday, July 24, at 5 PM</strong>, give to your favorite local nonprofits through a single donation, supported by a&nbsp;<strong>pooled matching grant</strong>&nbsp;from generous businesses and individual Challengers. This means your gift goes further to help the critical work and impact of the causes you care about most.</p>

<p><em>“Whether you’ve lived here for decades or recently moved to Teton Valley, this is an exciting opportunity to be part of something meaningful,”</em> said Bonnie Self, Executive Director of the Community Foundation. <em>“Every gift supports critical causes and raises vital funds for organizations that make our community stronger.”</em></p>

<h3><strong>Why it Matters</strong></h3>

<p>Engaging one in three households, the Tin Cup Challenge has raised more than&nbsp;<strong>$30.8 million</strong>&nbsp;for organizations across Teton Valley over the past 18 years. These funds support vital programs in education, healthcare, social services, conservation, animal welfare, the arts, recreation, and more. In 2025, the community helped raise&nbsp;<strong>$3.8 million</strong>&nbsp;invested throughout the valley, fueling the daily work that keeps our community thriving year-round.</p>

<p><strong>100% of your donation goes to the nonprofits you choose.</strong></p>

<h3><strong>How to participate</strong></h3>

<ol>
<li><strong>Give anytime during the 6-week Giving Period</strong>&nbsp;(June 12–July 24):
<ol>
<li>Online at&nbsp;<a href="http://www.tincupchallenge.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.TinCupChallenge.org</a></li>
<li>By check using the Tin Cup Donor Form you received in the mail</li>
<li>Via stock, wire transfer, or donor-advised fund</li>
<li>Visit us on Fridays at the Driggs Farmers Market from 9am–1pm</li>
<li>Stop by our office or use our drop box by the front door</li>
</ol>
</li>

<li><strong>Celebrate on Event Day</strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;<strong>Saturday, July 18 (9 am–Noon at the Driggs City Park)</strong>:
<ol>
<li>Register for 5K /10K races or the Fun Run/Walk</li>
<li>Enjoy free refreshments, live entertainment, and fun activities</li>
<li>Engage with local nonprofits and their leaders</li>
<li>Get your complimentary T-shirt&nbsp;<em>(while supplies last)</em></li>
</ol>
</li>

<li><strong>Become a Challenger ($1,500+) or Friend of the Match ($1–$1,499)</strong>
<ol>
<li>Grow the Match Grant for participating nonprofits</li>
<li>Fund Competitive Grants and Youth Philanthropy</li>
<li>Provide training opportunities for nonprofit leaders</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>

<h3><strong>New to the valley?</strong></h3>

<p>We invite all members of the community to explore the amazing work of more than&nbsp;<strong>70 local nonprofits</strong>&nbsp;and discover how you can make an impact. It’s a great way to connect with neighbors and align your passions with community needs. Look for the&nbsp;<strong>Tin Cup brochure in your mailbox on June 12</strong>, visit us online or at the&nbsp;<strong>Driggs Farmers Market</strong>&nbsp;on Fridays through July 24, or stop by our office (189 North Main Street, Suite 112) to donate, pick up your free T-shirt, or register to run!</p>

<p>The Community Foundation extends heartfelt gratitude to the Business and Community Challengers who have committed their support to this remarkable program. Together, we can ensure that Teton Valley remains a place where generosity and community thrive.</p>

<p><strong>Give Local. Give Together. Give Bigger.</strong><br>Visit&nbsp;<a href="http://www.tincupchallenge.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.TinCupChallenge.org</a>&nbsp;<strong>or call 208.354.0230 to learn more.</strong></p>

<hr>

<h3><strong>About the Community Foundation of Teton Valley</strong></h3>

<p>The mission of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley is to elevate lives through the power of generosity. It seeks to achieve its mission by championing the nonprofit community, empowering donors, promoting a culture of giving, and serving as a catalyst in addressing critical community needs. The Community Foundation also hosts the Tin Cup Challenge, an annual fundraiser that has raised nearly $30.8 million for Teton Valley nonprofits in just 18 years.</p>
